<title>USA: Indiana/Ohio direct hogs up $0.50/1.00 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Indiana/Ohio direct hogs up $0.50/1.00 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>SPRINGFIELD 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Barrows and gilts were mostly $.50 higher, some $1.00 higher. Demand was moderate to good on a light to moderate movement. Top $61.00 per cwt. - USDA</p>
<p>			  Country		 Plants</p>
<p>US 1-2  230-260 lbs 58.50-60.00	   59.50-61.00</p>
<p>		    Few 58.00 &amp; 60.50</p>
<p>US 2-3  230-260 lbs 54.00-58.00</p>
<p>	  210-230 lbs 49.50-54.00</p>
<p>Sows:  Steady to 1.00 Higher. Top 53.00.</p>
<p>US 1-3  300-450 lbs 44.00-46.00</p>
<p>	  450-500 lbs 45.50-48.00</p>
<p>	  500-600 lbs 47.50-52.00</p>
<p>Few over 600 lbs 52.00-53.00</p>
</text>
